+
+## 09-18 — defect (e) exhumed: VAES EVEX + vararg-.irp + .octa; three silent-corruption fixes; rebase to 352e0fd9
+
+Upstream moved: S06 merged as squashed `414475d7` (PR #550, main
+`352e0fd9`). The re-base was trivial this time — `git diff origin/main
+work` was empty, my branch content was byte-identical to main — so
+`checkout -B work origin/main` and a fastbuild rebuild (env: swap
+8 GiB still active, rustc 1.98.1, libc6-dev-i386 survived).
+
+**Kernel tree regeneration.** The wipe took the tarball, the
+CachyMod patch set, and most of the tree (30 of 91k files). Re-did:
+cdn.kernel.org tarball (154,741,268 B, xz -t clean), sparse
+archpkgbuilds clone (33 patches), `prepare_kernel_tree.sh`. The
+script's whole-tree audit refused to pass: `find -type f` under-counts
+the archive listing by exactly the tree's 85 symlinks, so it
+re-extracted forever. Fixed the count to `( -type f -o -type l )`
+in the same commit. Also reinstalled wiped host tools
+(bc/flex/bison/cpio/zstd/libelf-dev/libssl-dev/kmod).
+
+**Defect (e) root cause — four assembler defects, not one.** The
+reported error was "vaesenc: no AVX-512/EVEX form for these operands
+(zmm/k/masked)" on `aes-ctr-avx-x86_64.S` (aes_ctr64_crypt_vaes_avx512,
+VL=64 instantiation). GAS accepts and encodes `vaesenc %zmm` —
+EVEX.512.66.0F38.W0 — while lccc's VEX-only table rejected it. Fixing
+that (encode_evex_binary arms, map=2/pp=66/W0) opened the file and
+exposed the rest:
+
+1. **VAES EVEX gap** (the reported bug). GAS-parity detail learned the
+   hard way: VAES has NO opmask (`{%k1}{z}`) and NO embedded-broadcast
+   (`{1toN}`) forms — GAS rejects them, and lccc's generic EVEX binary
+   encoder would happily have set the mask/bcst bits into an invalid
+   instruction (objdump renders it `/(bad)`). New
+   `evex_forbid_mask_bcst` guard rejects with GAS's exact wording.
+2. **vpsrldq/vpslldq EVEX gap** — same operand classes, reused the
+   existing `encode_evex_shift_imm` (0F map, 73 /3 and /7, W0); also
+   no opmask/broadcast per GAS.
+3. **`:vararg` macro binding — the silent one.** `.macro _xor_data
+   vecs:vararg` + `.irp i, \vecs` (the file's AES round loops)
+   expanded `\vecs` to the FIRST argument only, in BOTH macro engines
+   (asm_preprocess::expand_macros and the x86 parser's GasMacro). One
+   of 8 iterations emitted: the object was missing 7/8 of its
+   vaesenc rounds, all vaesenclast/xor/store tails — no diagnostic,
+   valid ELF, would have passed straight into the kernel. Both
+   binders now join the remaining positional args (empty → ""). Root
+   cause: the qualifier was stripped and discarded at parse time;
+   nothing remembered which parameter was vararg.
+4. **`.octa` silently dropped** — unknown-directive fallthrough
+   emitted NOTHING for 16-byte constants; `.Lbswap_mask` vanished and
+   the pool shifted. (Same bug class the file already documents for
+   .float/.space.) New arm + u128 literal parser (hex/dec/bin/oct,
+   optional '-'), LE like GAS.
+
+**Gold-standard validation.** Byte-diff of lccc's
+`aes-ctr-avx-x86_64.o` vs GAS's (same tree, same preprocessor):
+.rodata identical; instruction stream identical modulo (a) the
+intentional commutative-vpxor VEX.2 shortening (1 byte shorter per
+instance, 7040→7136-byte .text delta explained) and (b) NOP padding
+style (90s vs nopl). 264/264 vaesenc/vaesenclast present in both.
+
+**Map-numbering lesson.** The repo's EVEX `map` parameter is
+1=0F/2=0F38/3=0F3A — VPADDQ/VPXORD EVEX live in the 0F map (SSE
+re-promotions), which is why "vpaddq is 0F38 in VEX" intuition
+misfires; decode GAS bytes before trusting arm patterns, mirror a
+proven arm (vpmulld for VAES, vpsraw for vpsrldq).
+
+**Regression coverage.** `tests/asm-diff/vaes.casefile` (6 groups:
+rounds/512/high-regs + reject groups for mask/broadcast),
+`tests/asm-diff/macro_vararg.casefile` (4 groups: kernel pattern,
+nested forwarding, single+empty invocation, head+rest). asm-diff
+against this box's GNU as 2.44: new binary 276 pre-existing failures
+(canonical 2.44-vs-2.47 alignment/padding differences — verified
+byte-identical failure set modulo my 10 new passing groups by running
+the stashed pre-change binary: 283 fails). cargo test 2865/0 (3 new
+unit tests for vararg binding). ci_local --fast 43/0/3 ALL GREEN.
+rustfmt gate caught one formatting miss — cargo fmt before re-run.
+
+**Next**: full bzImage rebuild with the fixed compiler (running),
+boot validation of defect (d) (expect no bad-pte BUG), then defect
+(b) CPU1 SIPI, then the CachyOS 6.18 LTS performance comparison.
